Z||000000||JohnnyK||06-02-2000||06:33 PM||||Fairly easy to weld a new support into the engine carriage where the a-arm connects to it? (rusted through) for a backyard mechanic? I heard that it is 4 wheel alignment, so does this give me enough room for error?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowCG||06-02-2000||09:54 PM||||If there's bad rust anywhere else,I might try and find a replacement cradle.<BR>If the control arm is in good shape,then you could use it to locate the plate you weld in by bolting a plate to it,then tack welding to the subframe,remove the control arm,and finish the weld.Since it'd be difficult to weld inside the subframe,maybe a formed piece,plug-welded from the top and bottom would work better.||||reg||1
